        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Decision Rule",
          "text": "Single-row invariant: atomic UPDATE. Cross-row invariant: Serializable or a materialized lock row. Uniqueness or overlap: a real DB constraint, always preferred over transaction ceremony."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "When MVCC Isn't Enough",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "MVCC handles reads. Explicit locks handle the cases where you must serialize writers by hand."
        },
